What I especially want to test is whether a model using these recovered connections can solve an unfamiliar problem better than the same model without them.

That gives us a falsifiable test of whether the instructions between the lines contain transferable value.

And it returns us to the pact.

A marker points to something. A shovel lets you investigate. A bridge joins what you’ve uncovered. A successful test turns the discovery into another tool.

The repository doesn’t have to be finished before it’s useful. In fact, some of its future value may come from what earlier readers deliberately—or accidentally—left unfinished.

